      "id": 1,
      "text": "McConnellsburg was laid out by Daniel McConnell on April 20, 1786, and his log cabin still stands in the borough’s historic core.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McConnellsburg%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough officially incorporated on March 26, 1814, becoming the county seat of Fulton County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McConnellsburg%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1993 the McConnellsburg Historic District, with 144 contributing buildings, was listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McConnellsburg%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "McConnellsburg sits in a 2‑mile‑wide valley between Tuscarora Mountain to the east and Little Scrub Ridge to the west.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McConnellsburg%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Today the largest employer in McConnellsburg is Oshkosh Corporation’s JLG Industries, a leading maker of boomlifts and other construction equipment.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
